ons as test failures. Instead, allow them\0A      to crash the program or throw a pop-up (on Windows).\0A\0AExcept for @G--gtest_list_tests@D, you can alternatively set the corresponding\0Aenvironment variable of a flag (all letters in upper-case). For example, to\0Adisable colored text output, you can either specify @G--gtest_color=no@D or set\0Athe @GGTEST_COLOR@D environment variable to @Gno@D.\0A\0AFor more information, please read the Google Test documentation at\0A@Ghttp://code.google.com/p/googletest/@D. If you find a bug in Google Test\0A(not one in your own code or tests), please report it to\0A@G<googletestframework@@googlegroups.com>@D.\0A\00", align 16
